Mesa 25.0.x src/c11: do not define call_once and once_flag where glibc does

Mesa 25.0.7 defines once_flag and call_once unconditionally. A glibc that
defines them too (it sets __once_flag_defined) conflicts with that, so the
tree does not build on this host. drm_shim_ref.sh applies this patch only to a
Mesa tree that lacks the guard, to build the 25.0.7 shim driver that is
compared with the board.

Source: a backport of the guard in Mesa 26.2.1 src/c11/threads.h (line 121,
`#ifndef __once_flag_defined`, in third_party/mesa-26.2.1/) to 25.0.7's
src/c11/threads.h and src/c11/impl/threads_posix.c. Mesa is MIT licensed, so
the patch is MIT too. It changes no compiler or driver code.

Applies to the tarball tree with `patch -p1` from its root.

--- a/src/c11/impl/threads_posix.c
+++ b/src/c11/impl/threads_posix.c
@@ -46,12 +46,13 @@
 
 /*--------------- 7.25.2 Initialization functions ---------------*/
 // 7.25.2.1
+#ifndef __once_flag_defined
 void
 call_once(once_flag *flag, void (*func)(void))
 {
     pthread_once(flag, func);
 }
-
+#endif
 
 /*------------- 7.25.3 Condition variable functions -------------*/
 // 7.25.3.1
--- a/src/c11/threads.h
+++ b/src/c11/threads.h
@@ -118,8 +118,10 @@
 typedef pthread_t       thrd_t;
 typedef pthread_key_t   tss_t;
 typedef pthread_mutex_t mtx_t;
+#ifndef __once_flag_defined
 typedef pthread_once_t  once_flag;
 #  define ONCE_FLAG_INIT PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT
+#endif
 #  ifdef PTHREAD_DESTRUCTOR_ITERATIONS
 #    define TSS_DTOR_ITERATIONS PTHREAD_DESTRUCTOR_ITERATIONS
 #  else
